                <pb facs="0296" n="1030" sameAs="frus:frus1895p2/pg1030"/>

                <head>
                    <hi rendition="#italic">Mr. Baker to Mr. Gresham.</hi>
                </head>
                <opener><seg rendition="#center">[Telegram.]</seg></opener>
                <opener><dateline rendition="#float-right"><placeName><hi rendition="#small-caps"
                                >San Jose</hi></placeName>, <date calendar="gregorian"
                            when="1895-04-24"><hi rendition="#italic">April 24,
                        1895</hi></date>.</dateline></opener>
                <p>The minister for foreign affairs of Nicaragua telegraphs me three British vessels
                    are at Corinto to collect indemnity, which Nicaragua can not pay. Great Britain
                    refused postponement or arbitration.</p>
                <closer>
                    <signed>
                        <hi rendition="#small-caps">Baker.</hi>
                    </signed>
                </closer>
            </div>
        </body>
    </text>
